# From or in the [[countryside]] or connected with it.
#* {{RQ:Churchill Celebrity|chapter=5|passage=When this conversation was repeated in detail within the hearing of the young woman in question, and undoubtedly for his benefit, Mr. Trevor threw shame to the winds and scandalized the Misses Brewster then and there by proclaiming his father to have been a '''country''' storekeeper.}}
# Of or connected to [[country music]].
# {{lb|en|India|historical}} Originating in [[India]] rather than being imported from [[Europe]] or elsewhere.
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1872|title=Silk in India|page=16
|passage=We have seen that the Company manufactured silk stuffs at three of its Residencies, but from '''country'''-wound silk.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1884|title=Journal of the United Service Institution of India|page=185
|passage=A reference to the Annual Administration Reports of the Department of Horse-breeding Operations {{...}} will allow of the opinion being arrived at, that the breed of '''country''' horses under the present regime is steadily improving.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1937|author=Brigadier-General H. A. Young|title=The East India Company’s Arsenals & Manufactories
|passage='''Country''' harness costs nearly as much, lasts half the time, and is in every respect inferior. It is understood that the only reason is that the Court desires to improve and encourage Indian manufactures.}}

